    "title": {
      "en": "Blizzard Addressing Issue with Nebulous Voidcores for Players Who Were Temporarily Suspended",
      "es": "Blizzard soluciona el problema de los núcleos vacíos nebulosos para los jugadores que fueron suspendidos temporalmente"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Blizzard Addressing Issue with Nebulous Voidcores for Players Who Were Temporarily Suspended...",
      "es": "Blizzard aborda el problema con los núcleos vacíos nebulosos para los jugadores que fueron suspendidos temporalmente..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6ad0fbf0748055.79248599\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">Blizzard has announced an upcoming fix for players who picked up too many Bonus Rolls last week, as they can no longer get more at the moment.<br><br>When Bonus Rolls went live last week, players were able to turn in the Bonus Roll quest multiple times. Players who did this were <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/blizzard-temporarily-suspending-players-with-more-bonus-rolls-than-intended-383275\" data-contiguous=\"true\">temporarily suspended</a> while Blizzard removed the extra Bonus Rolls. Now, these players have reported that Blizzard didn't correctly fix their Bonus Roll tracker for the season, making them unable to pick up extra Bonus Rolls with each week as the game thinks they've already obtained too many. <br><br>Blizzard has announced that they are working on a fix for affected players.<div class=\"quote-box exclude-units last\" data-type=\"blizzard\" data-has-links=\"true\" data-has-source=\"true\" data-has-toggle=\"true\"><div class=\"quote-source\">Blizzard</div><div class=\"quote-header\"><a href=\"https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/2381342/22\" target=\"_blank\">View Original</a><a class=\"quote-toggle\" href=\"javascript:\" aria-label=\"Toggle quote visibility\"></a></div><div class=\"quote-body\" data-markup-content-target=\"1\">We are working on a fix for players who received more Nebulous Voidcores than intended and then had them removed.</div></div></div>\n            \n            <noscript>Blizzard has announced an upcoming fix for players who picked up too many Bonus Rolls last week, as they can no longer get more at the moment.<br /><br />When Bonus Rolls went live last week, players were able to turn in the Bonus Roll quest multiple times. Players who did this were <a href=\"https://www.wowhead.com/news/blizzard-temporarily-suspending-players-with-more-bonus-rolls-than-intended-383275\">temporarily suspended</a> while Blizzard removed the extra Bonus Rolls. Now, these players have reported that Blizzard didn't correctly fix their Bonus Roll tracker for the season, making them unable to pick up extra Bonus Rolls with each week as the game thinks they've already obtained too many. <br /><br />Blizzard has announced that they are working on a fix for affected players. <br /><br /><div class=\"quote-box\" data-type=\"blizzard\"><div class=\"quote-header\"></div><div class=\"quote-body\">We are working on a fix for players who received more Nebulous Voidcores than intended and then had them removed.</div></div></noscript>            \n        ",
